   "author": "89c9fc822e34b78c",
   "date": "2013-09-22T07:44:27Z",
   "subject": "Re: how to stop lavaan from ordering my variables?",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On 09/22/2013 02:48 AM, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oolve...@gmail.com</a> wrote:\r<br>&gt; hello. quick question. how can i force lavaan to keep my variables in\r<br>&gt; the order in which i entered them? is it possible? for example:\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "The order of the variables is based on the way you have specified your \r<br>model. The lavaan approach is to ignore the data as long as possible: we \r<br>parse your model syntax, figure out what is observed and what is latent, \r<br>and construct a parameter table. Only when we proceed with fitting the \r<br>model, we compute the needed sample statistics based on the data.\r<br>\r<br>You can &#39;see&#39; the parameter table by typing\r<br>\r<br>parTable(fit)\r<br>\r<br>The &#39;order&#39; of the observed variables is determined by the output of\r<br>\r<br>lavNames( parTable(fit), type=&quot;ov&quot; )\r<br>\r<br>BTW, the equivalent of\r<br>\r<br>&gt;&gt;fitted.values(fit)$cov\r<br>\r<br>for the sample data is\r<br>\r<br>inspect(fit, &quot;sampstat&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>which will use the same order as fitted().\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
