  {
   "id": "XCY8oltiIvwJ",
   "from": "Yves Rosseel",
   "author": "89c9fc822e34b78c",
   "date": "2013-09-22T16:20:58Z",
   "subject": "Re: how to stop lavaan from ordering my variables?",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On 09/22/2013 01:02 PM, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oolve...@gmail.com</a> wrote:\r<br>&gt; so, if i understand correctly, there is no argumentnow that tells lavaan\r<br>&gt; &quot;respect the ordering of the variables in the original covaraince\r<br>&gt; matrix&quot;, am i right?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Indeed.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>\r<br>it seems like it prints first\r<br>&gt; the endogenous/dependent variables, followed by the indpendent/exogenous\r<br>&gt; ones in the order where they were specified in the structural equations.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "The order is the following:\r<br>\r<br>ov.ind\r<br>ov.y\r<br>ov.x\r<br>other\r<br>\r<br>where ov.ind are observed indicators, ov.y are dependent variables (but \r<br>not indicators), ov.x are exogenous variables, and other are everything \r<br>not included in the {<a href=\"http://ov.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ov.in&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792432605533000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Zkj07vdPWJS0g_PK9ACzr\">ov.in</a>, ov.y, ov.x}.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; just being curious here. i&#39;m going to be using lavaan to teach some\r<br>&gt; basic path analysis/sem and i was hoping that my students could compare\r<br>&gt; their model-implied covariance matrices with their observed covariance\r<br>&gt; matrices without needing to re-ordering them first so they match each\r<br>&gt; other exactly.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "You will need to reorder them first.\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
